# Dual-land / branching

Canonical doc: `docs/BRANCHING.md`. Skill: `dual-land-bugfix`.

While a `release/*` branch is active (e.g. `release/0.0.1`):

- Work on `feature/SBM-<id>-…` or `bugfix/SBM-<id>-…` — never commit directly on `develop` or `release/*`.
- Changes that belong on UAT and dev need **two MRs**: into `release/*` (→ UAT) and into `develop` (→ dev).
- Prefer opening those PRs over cherry-picking onto long-lived branches. Use `scripts/dual-land.sh` only as a fallback when the user asks.
- Do not push `develop` / `release/*` unless the user asks.
- Do not dual-land unrelated feature work onto the release train.
